        "metadata": {
            "kira_final": "Everything is set up and verified working:\n\n**Configuration:**\n- **Git server:** bare repo at `/git/server.git`, owned by user `user` (SSH access via `user@server:/git/server`)\n- **Deploy hook:** `/git/server.git/hooks/post-receive` runs `GIT_WORK_TREE=/var/www/html git checkout -f master` on every push to `master`\n- **Webserver:** nginx serving `/var/www/html` on port 8080\n- sshd and nginx are running; `server` resolves via `/etc/hosts`\n\n**Verified end-to-end** (simulating your workflow from a client clone):\n```\ngit clone → echo \"hello world\" > hello.html → commit → push origin master\ncurl http://server:8080/hello.html   →   \"hello world\"\n```\n\nYou can now run your exact commands from your machine — each push to `master` automatically deploys the files to the webserver.",
